\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Weakens Real; Dealers See Outflow \b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 22:31\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--A \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the Brazilian real (BRL) against the dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the session will post a net outflow of between $200 million and $300 million, but the dollar buying didn't affect prices much because Banco do Brasil was reportedly providing liquidity to banks that needed to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Banco do Brasil denies playing that role. \par \par \uc2  Early in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the mini-band in which the real and dollar trade. The new band values the dollar at BRL1.1670-1.1760, up 0.10 centavos from the previous BRL1.1660-1.1750. \par \par \uc2  In the spot market, the commercial dollar's buy rate also moved up 0.10 centavos from Monday's closing level. The dollar for 48-hour delivery closed with a buy rate of BRL1.1739 and a sell rate of BRL1.1740. \par \par \uc2  The real continues to be under pressure as loans made under \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Rule 63 mature. Analysts estimate that 35% to 40% of those loans, which peaked in March, are being rolled over in August. The redemption of the remaining bonds is putting pressure on the real. \par \par \uc2  As reported, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Gustavo Franco said Tuesday that the country might see more redemptions than originally expected as investors redeem maturing loans to buy Brazilian Brady bonds. \par \par \uc2  Brazilian Bradys, which trade in sympathy with Russian Principals, have taken a whack in recent sessions because of Russia's acute economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, Brazil's C-bonds gained 1 3/4 to 267 1/4  bid, while EIs climbed 1 1/4 to 77 bid. \par \par \uc2  In Brazil's money market, the average interbank rate, or CDI, slipped to 2.08% from 2.09% Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At its regular weekly auction, the Treasury placed 1.5 billion reals\par ($1=BRL1.17) worth of floating-rate bills known as LFTs. The 266-day\par bills mature May 12, 1999. The discount to the Selic rate, to which the\par bills are indexed, was close to zero.\par    -By Geraldo Samor; 55-21-580-9394; gsamor@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  18-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2031GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du8i007cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
