\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens On Outflow, No  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1998\par 23:12\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real (BRL) weakened Tuesday against the dollar on a likely outflow of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the spot market, the commercial dollar for 48-hour delivery closed with a buy rate of BRL1.1653 and a sell rate of BRL1.1655, leaving the midpoint average at BRL1.1654, up from Monday's BRL1.16435. \par \par \uc2  The Real opened at the lows 1.1650 and inched up to trade at 1.1663, but all the action was contained within the mini-band in which the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. The mini-band was last adjusted Friday to a buy rate of 1.1638 and a sell rate at 1.1720 reals. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said that there was a probable net outflow of U.S. dollars Tuesday, as occurred Monday. According to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, Monday's commercial dollar net outflow was of $178 million, a first after consecutive sessions of huge net inflow following the privatization of giant telecommunications holding Telebras last week. The net July inflow stood at $6.69 billion. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the money market, the average interbank rate, or CDI, fell to 2.12%\par from 2.13% Monday.\par    -By Mara Lemos; 55-11-813-1988; mlemos@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  04-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2112GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du84006k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\s