\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens Vs Dollar On Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 1998\par 22:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real weakened against the dollar Monday following an adjustment of the mini-band in which the two countries trade. \par \par \uc2  Early in the session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the real - as it normally does every two to five working days - by slightly modifying the crawling band. \par \par \uc2  "The market had been expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the past two sessions," one Rio de Janeiro dealer said. "So the market factored that in already at the end of last week." \par \par \uc2  The new band values the dollar at 1.1580-1.1660 reals (BRL), up 0.15 centavos from the BRL1.1565-1.1645 previously. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar's buy rate at close was BRL1.1580 reals and the sell rate was BRL1.1581, leaving the midpoint average at BRL1.15805, up from 1.1567 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again later Monday to buy dollars at BRL1.1580. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that trading volume was the lowest it had been in recent memory, adding that they expect the trend to continue in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "The premiums are very low on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, so we're not expecting much improvement any time soon," the same dealer said. "And if there's any bad news abroad, things may even get a bit worse." \par \par \uc2  Traders said, however, that the local commercial dollar market may have shown a slight inflow Monday. \par \par \uc2  According to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, the commercial dollar market showed a net outflow of $120 million on Friday. The floating-rates market had a net outflow of $25 million. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the money market, the average interbank rate, or CDI, closed Monday\par unchanged, at 2.22%.\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; (5511) 813-1988; swisnefski@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2032GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7605or4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
