\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens Slightly; No  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 1998\par 20:11\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real (BRL) weakened slightly against the dollar Friday in below-average trading volume. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a mini-band adjustment by some market players led the dollar to surge as high as BRL1.1573 in early trade, but as it became clear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sit tight, the dollar retrenched a bit. \par \par \uc2  Late in Sao Paulo, the dollar for 48-hour delivery closed with a buy rate of BRL1.1566 and a sell rate of BRL1.1568, leaving the midpoint average at BRL1.15670, slightly higher than Thursday's BRL1.15660. \par \par \uc2  The mini-band values the dollar at BRL1.1565-1.1645. \par \par \uc2  Friday's traded volume fell 20% below the daily average, as the market slowed down ahead of the Brazil-Denmark World Cup match, scheduled for 1900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  On the capital-flow front, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed a net inflow of $33 million on the commercial market Thursday, and a net outflow of $129 million on the floating-rates market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the money market, the average interbank rate, or CDI, ended flat at\par 2.22%.\par    -By Geraldo Samor; 55-21-580-9394; gsamor@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  03-07-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1811GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du73004xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
