\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 214 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1998\par 21:10\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real (BRL) weakened against the dollar Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the mini-band in which the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was quiet ahead of the Brazil-Morocco World Cup match scheduled for 1900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The market was operating in a `I'm-going-home' mode," said a head trader in a Sao Paulo bank. "No one wanted to do anything extraordinary because they just wanted to watch the game." \par \par \uc2  Volume, however, was heavier than Monday, with $6.9 billion changing hands in the commercial exchange market, compared to $5.9 billion Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the commercial-exchange market, the dollar for 48-hour delivery closed with a buy rate of BRL1.1545 and a sell rate of BRL1.1546. \par \par \uc2  The midpoint average was BRL1.15455, slightly up from Monday's close of BRL1.15355. \par \par \uc2  Early in the session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjusted the mini-band to BRL1.1545/1.1615, up from BRL1.1535/1.1605 previously. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data show a net inflow of $109 million on the commercial market Monday, while the floating-rates market posted a net outflow of $97 million. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  16-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1910GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du6g003uj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
