\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Ends Firm \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1998\par 23:21\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--A regular \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the Brazilian real (BRL) Tuesday, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at the strongest point of its newly set crawling band. \par \par \uc2  With Brazil's World Cup debut Wednesday and a national holiday on Thursday making this a shorter business week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently decided to concentrate its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves on Tuesday's auction. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjusted the real's mini-band by 0.15 centavo, dribbling the market's expectation of a 0.10 centavo devaluation. \par \par \uc2  At the end of the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought excess dollars in the market. \par \par \uc2  The commercial buy rate at close was BRL1.1535, which is also the mini-band's bottom. The sell rate was BRL1.1536, leaving the midpoint average at BRL1.15355, up from Monday's BRL1.15260. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed a net inflow of $90 million on the commercial market Monday, while the floating-rates market had net outflow of $87 million. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the average interbank rate ended flat at 2.29%. \par \par \uc2  In other market developments Tuesday: \par \par \uc2  -- The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed BRL6 billion worth of floating-rate bills at the weekly Treasury auction. A similar auction will take place Wednesday, with BRL17 billion of bills going on the block. \par \par \uc2  -- Brazil posted a trade surplus of $283 million in the June 1-7 period, the Ministry of Trade and Industry said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -- Stocks closed lower. The benchmark Bovespa index fell 1.6%.\par   --By Geraldo Samor; 55-21-580-9394; gsamor@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  09-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2121GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010917du69003g2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
