\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Calm Day \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 23:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--Capping a nervous week on a positive note, the Brazilian real (BRL) weakened against the dollar Friday but closed at the strongest point of its crawling band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the crawling band early in the day. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that, aside from that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't seem to be trying to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this week, traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have sold up to $1 billion to drag down the dollar's exchange rate, which was taking off amid nervousness surrounding emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  On the commercial exchange market, the dollar for 48-hour delivery closed Friday at BRL1.1500/1.1502, at the bottom of the newly established mini-band. \par \par \uc2  The midpoint rate was BRL1.15035, up from Thursday's BRL1.1497. \par \par \uc2  The new mini-band values the dollar at BRL1.1500/1.1570, up from the previous BRL1.1490/1.1560. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the commercial-exchange market appeared to show a net inflow of dollars on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data show a net outflow of $78 million Thursday, while the floating-rates market saw a net outflow of $112 million. \par \par \uc2  In the money markets, the average interbank rate fell to 2.31% from 2.33% Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The decline reflects the market's high liquidity after the government\par on Tuesday decided not to place National Treasury Notes, or LTNs, with\par maturities up to one year. Banks were demanding rates so shigh that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decided to hold on to the bills.\par    --By Geraldo Samor; 55-21-580-9394; gsamor@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2107GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5t04myb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
