\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Dlr Outflow \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 1998\par 23:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real (BRL) weakened against the dollar Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's crawling band. \par \par \uc2  Even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move, the dollar failed to retreat to the bottom of the mini-band - signaling that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues in high demand. \par \par \uc2  On the commercial exchange market, the dollar for 48-hour delivery hit a high of BRL1.1518 and didn't pull back much. \par \par \uc2  The buy rate at close was BRL1.1515 and the sell rate was BRL 1.1517 for a midpoint of BRL1.1516, up from Thursday's BRL1.1492. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mini-band adjustment valued the dollar at BRL1.1485-1.1545, up from the previous BRL1.1475-1.1535. \par \par \uc2  There are a number of factors making the dollar a rarer commodity than it was in previous months. \par \par \uc2  No big privatization auctions are scheduled for this month, reducing the prospect of foreign direct investment in May. Also, after six consecutive cuts in the domestic interest rate, hot money is looking for other harbors, analysts here say. \par \par \uc2  As of Thursday, Brazil was registering a net outflow of $539 million this month, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data quoted by the Estado news agency. \par \par \uc2  The figure takes into account the $1.89 billion inflow in the commercial-exchange market and the $2.4 billion outflow in the floating-rates market. \par \par \uc2  In the money markets, the average monthly interbank rate (CDI) continued to dip after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered domestic rates on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The CDI closed at an annual 2.33%, down from 2.34% Thursday.\par    -By Geraldo Samor; 55-21-580-9394; gsamor@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2123GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5m04egc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
