\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Steady Vs Dlr, No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 April 1998\par 22:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real was steady against the dollar in calm trade Monday in a day without any \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar's buy rate at close was 1.1392 reals (BRL) ($1=BRL1.13) and the sell rate was BRL1.1393, leaving the midpoint average at BRL1.13925, slightly higher than the BRL1.1390 on Wednesday, the last trading day before the Easter holidays. \par \par \uc2  A Rio de Janeiro trader said the market is expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the real by 0.10 of a centavo against the dollar on Tuesday with one of its regular adjustments to the mini-band. \par \par \uc2  Last Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the mini-band by 0.10 of a centavo to BRL1.390-1.440 to the dollar from the previous BRL1.1380-1.1430. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars at BRL1.1390 and sells them at BRL1.1440. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market appeared to have shown a net inflow of dollars Monday, but a much smaller amount than in recent days. \par \par \uc2  In the interbank market, the average monthly interbank rate (CDI) dipped to 2.92% from 2.93% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Mary Milliken; (55-11) 813-1988; mmilliken@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-04-98 \par \par \uc2  2011GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du4d032et\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
