\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1998\par 22:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real was weaker against the dollar Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the mini-band in which the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  But the real remained at the strongest point of the mini-band as large dollar inflows continued to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  'It was a calm day on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with no impact from the other markets,' said a Rio de Janeiro trader referring to the large drop in Brazil's stock prices. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar's buy rate at close was 1.1380 reals (BRL) ($1=BRL1.13) and the sell rate was BRL1.1381, leaving the midpoint average at BRL1.13805, up from BRL1.13805 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  Early in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the mini-band by 0.10 of a centavo to BRL1.380-1.430 to the dollar from the BRL1.1370-1.1420 set last Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars at BRL1.1380 and sells them at BRL1.1430. \par \par \uc2  The commercial market showed net inflows of $575 million on Thursday, bringing the total for the first two days of the month to $900 million following the record net inflow of $11.95 billion in all of March. \par \par \uc2  In the interbank market, the average monthly interbank rate (CDI) rose to 2.90% from 2.87% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Mary Milliken; (55-11) 813-1988; mmilliken@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswi