\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Market Lifts The Real \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 22:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--As March draws to a close, sporadic signs of weakness in the Brazilian real only appear when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following its long-standing policy, moves to devalue the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That's what happened again Friday, when the real weakened in the morning - as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjusted the crawling band - only to bounce back up in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars late in the day to prevent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from dropping below the mini-band floor. But that wasn't much help, either. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar's buy rate at close was a notch below the mini-band's, at 1.1359 reals (BRL). The sell rate was BRL1.1361, and the midpoint average of BRL1.1360, up from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The mini-band now values the dollar at 1.1360-1.1410 reals (BRL), up 0.05 centavos from the BRL1.1355-1.1405 previously. \par \par \uc2  Net dollar inflows, which had slowed down last week, recovered their pace Thursday as $715 million entered Brazil via the commercial market, following a $604 million inflow on Wednesday. March net inflows stand now at a whopping $7.9 billion. \par \par \uc2  In fact, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  feels so comfortable with those figures that Thursday it moved to close a window commonly used by hot money to get into the country - the so-called Resolution 63, which allows borrowing overseas for domestic agricultural investments. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank market, the average monthly interbank rate (CDI)\par closed unchanged at 2.89%.\par    -By Geraldo Samor; 55-21-580-9394; gsamor@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-03-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2111GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3r02nwc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
