\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Ends Weaker After Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 22:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real closed weaker against the dollar Wednesday following a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the mini-band in which the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar buy rate at close was 1.1308 reals and the sell rate was 1.1312 reals, for a midpoint of 1.1310, up from Tuesday's closing mark of 1.1303. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  every three to five working days to weaken the real against the dollar, set the new band at 1.1310-1.1360 reals, up from the previous 1.1300-1.1350 reals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in Wednesday's session to purchase excess dollars at 1.1310 reals. \par \par \uc2  A heavy inflow of foreign capital continues to sustain the domestic market, traders said. On Tuesday, the commercial exchange market registered a net inflow of $813 million. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market showed a net inflow of $5 billion in February. Analysts said foreign capital inflow may slow in March if interest rates are reduced, as expected. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's Monetary Policy Committee is meeting late Wednesday to set rates. Market watchers have estimated that the annual prime lending rate will drop to 30%, from the current 34.5%. \par \par \uc2  'In the short term I think we could see a reduced level of capital inflow because of the new rates,' one Rio de Janeiro trader said. 'But foreign cash inflow will be even higher starting in April and May because of privatizations.' \par \par \uc2  The expectation for a rate cut pressured the interbank market Wednesday, as the average monthly interbank rate (CDI) plunged to 3.00% from 3.42% \par \par \uc2  -By Stephen Wisnefski; (5511) 813 1988; swisnefski@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-03-98 \par \par \uc2  2112GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3401xi5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
