\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weaker After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 1998\par 20:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real closed weaker against the dollar Friday following a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the mini-band in which the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar buy rate at close was 1.1300 reals and the sell rate was 1.1301 reals, for a midpoint of 1.13005, up from Thursday's closing mark of 1.1291. \par \par \uc2  As had been expected, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early during Friday's session to weaken the real by adjusting the band, as it does every three to five working days. \par \par \uc2  The new band values the dollar at 1.1300-1.1350 reals. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now buys dollars at 1.1300 and sells them at 1.1350 reals. \par \par \uc2  The mini-band lies within a larger wide-band that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seldom modifies. The wide band was set at 1.12-1.22 reals per dollar on Jan. 20, after being at 1.05-1.14 for nearly a year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again late Friday to purchase excess dollars at the pre-determined 1.1300 reals. \par \par \uc2  Bucking the recent trend, the exchange market showed a net outflow on Thursday. The commercial market registered a net outflow of $143 million, while the floating market had a net outflow of $79 million. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they are not concerned about Thursday's outflow, noting that they continue to expect a heavy inflow of foreign capital. With Friday's figures still to be included in this month's final figure, the commercial and floating markets have shown a net inflow of $4.7 billion in February. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank market, the average monthly interbank rate (CDI)\par closed steady at 3.46%.\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; (5511) 813 1988; swisnefski@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1936GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2r01rld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
