\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weaker Vs Dlr; 3 Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 1998\par 20:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real weakened against the dollar Friday following a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust the mini-band in which the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar buy rate closed at 1.1248 reals and the sell rate was 1.1252 reals, for a midpoint of 1.1250, the floor of the new trading mini-band. The dollar closed Thursday at 1.12405 reals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the real early in Friday's session by adjusting the trading band, as it does every three to five working days. \par \par \uc2  The new band values the dollar at 1.1250-1.1300 reals, up from the previous 1.1240-1.1290 reals. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now buys dollars at 1.1250 and sells them at 1.1300 reals. \par \par \uc2  The mini-band lies within a larger wide-band that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seldom modifies. The wide band was set at 1.12-1.22 reals per dollar on January 20, after being at 1.05-1.14 for nearly a year. \par \par \uc2  In addition to adjusting the mini-band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  two times near the end of Friday's session to buy excess dollars - as has been the norm this week - at the pre-determined 1.1250 reals. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Thursday that the country's reserves had increased by $2 billion since the beginning of the year to $54 billion. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's commercial exchange market showed a net inflow of $386 million on Thursday while the floating market posted a net outflow of $50 million. Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flow figures are released with a delay of one working day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank market, the average monthly interbank rate (CDI)\par closed steady at 3.52%.\par -By Stephen Wisnefski; (5511) 813 1988; swisnefski@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 06-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1916GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du26011jf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
