\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weaker After Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 1998\par 20:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real was a touch weaker Tuesday after a slow trading day in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the market, said traders. \par \par \uc2  "The market was quiet because of the holiday in Rio (de Janeiro), which accounts for 30% of our business," said a trader with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar buy rate closed at 1.1199 reals and the sell rate was 1.1201 reals, for a midpoint of 1.1200, up from 1.1192 at Monday's close. The real weakened as far as 1.1204 during the day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were contained within the trading "mini-band," which was adjusted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the day, as it does regularly. The new band values the dollar at 1.1200-1.1250 reals, up 0.10 centavos from the previous band that ranged at 1.1190-1.1240 reals. \par \par \uc2  The mini-band lies within a larger 'wide band' that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seldom modifies. \par \par \uc2  The 'wide band' was set at 1.05-1.14 reals per dollar on Feb. 18, 1997 after more than a year at 0.97-1.06 reals per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The trader also said the holiday in the U.S. Monday contributed to the weakening of the real, since market participants who weren't selling dollars Monday were back on the market Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also held a sell auction later Monday and bought reals at 1.1200. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank market, 