\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Forex \highlight\uc2 :Real Slightly Stronger After Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 1998\par 20:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real was slightly stronger Friday with limited market fluctuations after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the session, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "After the spread auction, the market was really quiet with no major moves," said one Rio de Janeiro trader. \par \par \uc2  The commercial dollar buy rate closed at 1.1198 reals and the sell rate was 1.1200 reals, for a midpoint of 1.1199, down from 1.1201 at Thursday's close. The real weakened as far as 1.1213 during the day. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were contained within the new trading "mini-band" as adjusted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, as it does regularly. The new band values the dollar at 1.1190-1.1240 reals, up 0.10 centavos from the previous band that ranged at 1.1180-1.1230 reals. \par \par \uc2  The mini-band lies within a larger 'wide band' that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seldom modifies. \par \par \uc2  The 'wide band' was set at 1.05-1.14 reals per dollar on Feb. 18, 1997 after more than a year at 0.97-1.06 reals per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the real market has been floating amid thin volume in the past week because participants are still aprehensive as a consequence of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equities' markets turmoil. \par \par \uc2  "But this week there was less of an impact than expected, despite the declarations of Soros," he said, referring to investor George Soros, who said the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis would spill over to Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interbank market, the average monthly interbank rate (CDI) rose\par to 3.81% from 3.83%.\par -By Mara Lemos; (55-11) 813-1988; mlemos@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-01-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1938GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1g00fch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
