\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Malan -2: Buying Dollars Friday And Monday \b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1997\par 21:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO (AP-Dow Jones)--Brazil Finance Minister Pedro Malan said Monday that the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market against the real on Friday and Monday is a sign that investor confidence is returning in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Malan, who spoke to the press after appearing at an Inter-American Development Bank conference in Santiago, said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar buying to keep the real from breaking through the strong side of the mini-band "is a sign that the (financial) situation is moving towards normalization." \par \par \uc2  In the face of a massive sell-off of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by investors spooked by the Asian financial crisis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to aggressively sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in late October and early November to keep the real from falling through the weak side of the mini-band. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-12-97 \par \par \uc2  2028GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc1097rl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
