\par\par \b \uc2  Brady Bonds Close Up; Moderate Volume As Investors Return \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1997\par 23:31\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Brady bonds are closing higher\par Monday following the Dow Jones Industrial Average amid\par moderate volumes as investors return from the long weekend,\par traders said.\par    "Unless a major announcement - like a Japanese brokerage\par house or a bank collapse - we expect the upside trend to\par continue tomorrow. Volumes are back up, but it's mainly\par dealer driven, as investors are returning slowly," a trader\par said.\par    When asked about the market's reaction to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy dollars Friday and Monday,\par he said it was perceived as a very positive sign because\par there's excess U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Brazilian market .\par    "The real was becoming too strong which could hurt\par exports. The bank wanted to keep the real from breaking\par through the stronger side of the band at which it trades,"\par he explained.\par    At 2142 GMT, Brazilian Pars added 1 1/4 to 70 bid, EIs\par climbed 1 1/8 to 85 5/8 bid, and C bonds gained 1 1/4 to 76\par bid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  12-01-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1731EST \par \par \uc2  1179 1810 4057 4071 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtc102l6j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
