\par\par \b \uc2  France's BNP opens subsidiary in Brazil. \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Nov 11 (Reuters) - France's Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP) on Tuesday inaugurated a fully-owned Brazilian subsidiary in a move that completes its network in the Latin American region, the bank's Chairman said. \par \par \uc2  "By setting up this bank in Brazil, BNP will complete its presence in Latin America," Michel Pebereau told a news conference, noting that BNP is already present in Argentina, Uruguay, Chile, Peru, Colombia, Venezuela, Mexico, Panama, Costa Rica and the Cayman Islands. \par \par \uc2  Though officially inaugurated Tuesday, the BNP subsidiary has been operating since May 1997, less than six months after the French bank was authorized by the Brazilian authorities to start business in the country. \par \par \uc2  BNP, which has been present in Brazil for the last 40 years through a representative office, began its investments by absorbing private bank Banco Comercial de Sao Paulo which was under \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With initial capital of $60 million, the BNP \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit aims to offer all types of services provided by commercial and investment banks, including trade financing, treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  products, focusing on institutional and corporate clients, Pebereau said. \par \par \uc2  He also said that over the next few weeks the bank plans to begin offering asset management services, which will allow it to also include individual clients in its portfolio. \par \par \uc2  BNP currently manages over $50 billion in investment funds worldwide. \par \par \uc2  Despite current worries about the Brazilian economy, Pebereau said the bank is optimistic about investing in the country and praised the steps taken by the government to face the difficulties following recent global financial turmoil. \par \par \uc2  "The Brazilian response by accelerating the fiscal adjustment shows the country is adapting itself to face the market turbulence," he said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the government unveiled a package of 51 tough fiscal measures designed to guarantee its defenses against global financial instability. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the government is taking the necessary measures, I don't see reason why the turbulence should last longer," Pebereau added. \par \par \uc2  BNP has been given the right to open 10 branches in Brazil. Its second office - the bank is headquarted in Sao Paulo - was likely to be open in Rio de Janeiro in the beginning of next year. \par \par \uc2  -- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412 \par \par \uc2  E-mail: fatima.santos@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbb02qro\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
