\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real weak despite  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Nov 7 (Reuters) - A series of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday failed to take pressure off the Brazilian real amid strong dollar demand due to next week's U.S. holiday and worries over weak global stock markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very nervous. Even after the auctions, there is still strong dollar demand," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held three dollar sell auctions in the commercial and floating exchange rate markets before lunch to bring the real back into the real-dollar mini-band of 1.1035-1.1085 reais per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The real was trading at 1.1086 reais per dollar prior to the auctions, when the bank sold dollars at 1.1085 reais. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the real back into the mini-band, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still trading at the ceiling of the band, indicating weakness, traders said. \par \par \uc2  When the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closed for lunch at 1300 local time/1500 GMT/1000 EST, the real was trading at 1.1085 reais per dollar, off 0.09 percent over the open of 1.1075 reais. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that amid the nervousness, Friday's scheduled auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-indexed NBC-E bonds in the afternoon might not calm markets as much as it normally does. \par \par \uc2  Auctions of the NBC-E bonds usually soothe the market because they signal that the government is not worried about taking on more dollar-indexed debt, something it would not do if it were mulling devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand grew Friday in the spot market ahead of the U.S. Veteran's Day holiday next Tuesday, which encouraged banks to buy dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was also nervous over falls on global stock exchanges, which shoved Brazil's stock market down around nine percent at the open. The bolsa later retreated from its worst levels to trade off around seven percent. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to jack up interest rates to an annualized 43 percent from about 20 percent after a week of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to prop up the real. \par \par \uc2  The rate hike gave solid support to the real this week through Thursday, when dollar outflows to pay Eurobond commitments pressured the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses the real-dollar mini-band to allow the real to trade within a controlled range against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Over the past two years, it has devalued the band slightly about five times a month to arrive at a nominal seven or eight percent depreciation of the real over the year. \par \par \uc2  ((-- John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511-248-5414)) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab    E-mail: john.miller@reuters.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (c) Reuters Limited 1997\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb702u1z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
