\par\par \b \uc2  Brady Bonds Track DJIA Lower; Concern Over South Korea \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1997\par 17:10\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Brady bonds continue to zig-zag Thursday morning amid growing concerns that a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might force South Korean banks to liquidate their holdings in emerging market debt. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won settled at an all-time low Thursday despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1600 GMT, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  C-bonds had lost 1 1/8 to 71 3/8 bid and 71 3/4 offered while the 2027 global bonds had shed 3/4 to 83 1/4 to 84 bid. \par \par \uc2  Argentine Pars were 1/2 lower at 69 bid and 69 1/2 offered while the 2027 globals had lost 2 to 86 bid and 87 1/8 offered. \par \par \uc2  Despite market concerns, traders said they hadn't seen South Korean banks dumping their emerging market debt holdings, estimated to total between $2.0 billion and $5.0 billion. \par \par \uc2  "The market was heading lower, and when the Dow opened, we followed it on a downward trend," a trader said. At 1600 GMT, the Dow Jones Industrial Average was down 0.39% at 7663. \par \par \uc2  Mexican Pars have slid 3/8 to 78 3/8 bid and 78 5/8 offered. The UMS 2026, meanwhile, had given up 1 15/16 to 110 1/4 bid and 111 offered. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market shrugged off the Venezuelan lower house's motion late\par Wednesday for a no-confidence vote against Finance Minister Luis Matos\par Azocar for allegedly mishandling a $4.0 billion Brady swap, traders\par said. Venezuelan Pars were off 5/8 at 83 5/8 bid and 83 7/8 offered\par while the DCBs were 1/4 lower to 88 3/4 bid and 89 offered.\par    -By Man Yin 