\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil spent $4-$5 bln to defend real - gov't aide. \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent between $4 billion and $5 billion of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves defending the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid market turmoil this week, presidential spokesman Sergio Amaral said Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "It has used between four and five billion dollars to withstand speculation against the real," Amaral told reporters during a daily briefing. "Reserves are there to be used when necessary." \par \par \uc2  "The president has total confidence in the measures that the economic team has taken to meet the speculation," the spokesman said. "What the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did was correct. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to take whatever measures necessary." \par \par \uc2  Amaral also said Brazil's trade deficit in October, excluding Friday, the last day of the month, was $760 million and "less than expected." \par \par \uc2  A latest Reuters survey of analysts forecast a trade deficit of about $1.24 billion in October. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over Brazil's trade gap and its currrent account deficit have contributed to questions about the country's ability to maintain the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Amaral said other indicators showed the Brazilian economy was "growing stronger by the day" and that the recent slump in local stocks was part of a wider, international problem. \par \par \uc2  The Bovespa index  .BVSP index of 51 leading shares fell 9.81 percent on Thursday, bringing its decline since last Friday to 23.3 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  four times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday to prop up the real. It also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  seven times on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Before this week's pressure, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at about $62 billion. \par \par \uc2  (( -- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 3141193)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtau03jdt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
