\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Brazil - Oct 29. \b0\par\par\uc2 384 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Oct 29 (Reuters) - These are the highlights of the main Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro newspapers this morning. \par \par \uc2  - - - \par \par \uc2  GAZETA MERCANTIL \par \par \uc2  -- \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  SECURES REAL, BOLSAS FOLLOW NEW YORK UP \par \par \uc2  With combined action in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks, the government managed to reverse the beginnings of panic in financial markets in the morning and close the day with shares higher and the exchange rate within the mini-band. \par \par \uc2  -- DERIVATIVES LOST MOST, FIXED INCOME UNDER LESS PRESSURE \par \par \uc2  Most Brazilian investors began the day yesterday with a smaller net worth than they had last week. Except for portfolios comprised exclusively of fixed-income paper, nearly all local investment funds fell in recent days, led by those which invest in derivatives. \par \par \uc2  -- COMMISSION CONFIRMS ENRON VICTORY \par \par \uc2  The purchase by Cia Hidreletrica Enron S.A. and Empresa Brasileira de Energia Ltda of 1,000 megawatts (MW) of electrical energy from Argentina was confirmed yesterday when a federal panel rejected an appeal by Spain's Endesa. \par \par \uc2  - - - \par \par \uc2  FOLHA DE SAO PAULO \par \par \uc2  -- NEW YORK, SAO PAULO BOLSAS RECOUP, CENBANK SECURES REAL \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The New York Stock Exchange on Tuesday closed up 4.71\tab  percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovering losses from the previous day's global equities meltdown. Sao Paulo's bolsa, which for the first time set limits to avoid a crash, surged 6.42 percent after plunging at the open.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -- BNDES STUDIES SMALLER PRIVATIZATION PREMIUMS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The president of the National Development Bank (BNDES), Luiz Carlos Mendonca de Barros, told Folha that the stock market could result in smaller privatization premiums than expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par O GLOBO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -- CENBANK CONTAINS DOLLAR SPECULATION, WORLD BOLSAS RISE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World markets took another historic turn Tuesday. Asian and Western bolsas awoke to record falls while in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and circuit breakers kept the financial market from crumbling before New York's spectacular rally reversed the trend and sent global equities soaring.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -- SON OF FORMER BRAZILIAN AMBASSADOR FOUND DEAD IN U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bernardo Gouthier, 45, the son of former Brazilian ambassador Hugo Gouthier, was found shot to death in front of his house in Indio, California, outside Los Angeles. Police are investigating the incident.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -- Reuters has not verified these stories and cannot vouch for their accuracy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((--James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --E-Mail: sao.paulo.newsroom@reuters.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (c) Reuters Limited 1997\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtat03goz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
