\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Cardoso Praises Nat Bank, Econ Team For Calming Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1997\par 16:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA (AP-Dow Jones)--Brazilian President Fernando Henrique Cardoso on Wednesday lauded the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government's economic team for taking the proper measures to tranquilize markets and stop a run on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real. \par \par \uc2  'Brazil has a very strong line of defense,' Cardoso told reporters outside the presidential palace in his first public comments on the market turmoil that hit stocks and the real Monday and Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'We have succeeded with tranquility in overcoming the difficult moment we went through yesterday, not only \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the entire world,' Cardoso added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  eight times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to keep the real within a pre-set band. Stock market regulators changed the trading hours to coincide with New York and introduced a circuit-breaker system. \par \par \uc2  Cardoso is the father of the 1994 economic stability program, the Real Plan, which has brought annual inflation down from 2700% in 1994 to an estimated 7% for 1997. \par \par \uc2  'The strength of our economy was proved once again yesterday (Tuesday),' said Cardoso. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1549GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtat084c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
