\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Weakens To 1.0964 Per Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 1997\par 22:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened Thursday, closing at 1.0964 to the dollar on a calm trading day with no \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the buy rate at close was 1.0963 reals per dollar and the sell rate was 1.0965 reals for a midpoint of 1.0964, a 0.0003 increase over Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  'It was a quiet day without major movements,' said one Rio de Janeiro broker, noting that the high point for the dollar Thursday was 1.0968. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to weaken the real against the dollar by adjusting the mini-band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades. \par \par \uc2  The new band values the dollar at 1.0960-1.1010 reals, up 0.05 of a centavo from the previous levels of 1.0955-1.1005 reals, set last Friday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will now buy dollars at 1.0960 reals per dollar and sell dollars at 1.1010 reals. \par \par \uc2  The change was made by shifting the mini band at which the real and dollar trade within the 1.05-1.14 reals per dollar wide band. \par \par \uc2  On April 23, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasted the real would be devalued by a total of around 7% during 1997. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-10-97 \par \par \uc2  2025GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dta207eg8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\png