\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Real Steady At 1.0956 Per Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 226 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1997\par 21:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-Dow Jones)--Brazil's real was steady on Monday, closing at 1.0956 to the dollar on a day with no \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the buy rate at close was 1.0955 reals per dollar and the sell rate was 1.0957 reals for a midpoint of 1.0956, or 0.00015 below Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  'The market is really quiet, especially considering that it's the end of the month,' said one Rio de Janeiro trader. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to weaken the real slightly against the dollar by adjusting the mini-band in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades. \par \par \uc2  The new band values the dollar at 1.0955-1.1005 reals, up 0.05 centavos from the previous levels of 1.0950-1.1000 reals, set last Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will now buy dollars at 1.0955 reals per dollar and sell dollars at 1.1005 reals. \par \par \uc2  The change was made by shifting the mini band at which the real and dollar trade within the 1.05-1.14 reals per dollar wide band. \par \par \uc2  On April 23, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecast the real would be devalued by a total of around 7% during 1997. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1958GMT \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9t07gbt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoa