\par\par \b \uc2  Latin America Stocks/Amplifier -2: Brazil Stand Praised \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1997\par 22:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'There hasn't been any substantial change in Brazil's macroeconomic situation,' said Sidney Chameh, head of research at Sao Paulo investment bank Banco Fator. 'We see no risk of an exchange devaluation.' \par \par \uc2  Around 2020 GMT, the real was steady, trading at 1.0806 to the dollar on a day with no \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Despite talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  can resort to tighter monetary policy to defend the real, Chameh said he expects to see a slight fall in interest rates in the second half of the year to reflect 'a significant fall in inflation,' now at an annualized 9%. \par \par \uc2  Mauro Schneider, ING Barings' senior economist for Brazil, said the possibility of a speculative attack on the real is quite low, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's present overvaluation makes it vulnerable to devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But he said that if the government decides to devalue the real, it would not do so before national elections in 1998. \par \par \uc2  Fabio Fukuda, analyst at Trend Analise Economica in Sao Paulo, said recent comments about changes in exchange policy, interest rates and current-account financing problems were used for speculative purposes. He praised the government of President Fernando Henrique Cardoso for reacting firmly to the speculation. \par \par \uc2  'The monetary authorities acted in an agile manner Tuesday by warning that there wouldn't be alterations in the exchange policy,' Fukuda said. 'That calmed the market.' \par \par \uc2  Some Brazilian investors are shell-shocked by Tuesday's fall, analysts said, and are likely to remain skittish for the rest of the week. \par \par \uc2  'The domestic funds were very much scared by the fall in the market,' said Fator's Chameh. \par \par \uc2  Fukuda noted that the hefty profit-taking 'breaks the bubble of super-optimistic expectations and brings us back to more realistic levels.' \par \par \uc2  In Argentina, the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange spent Wednesday's session following the recovering Brazilian markets, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  'The movements (Tuesday) and today were just because of Brazil,' said economist Raul Buonuome of Deutsche Morgan Grenfell in Buenos Aires. \par \par \uc2  After diving 3.4% on Tuesday, the blue-chip Merval Index recovered to close at 826.37, up 2.2%, in heavy trading. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-07-97 \par \par \uc2  2037GMT \par \par \uc2  1190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7g059e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
