\par\par \b \uc2  Unibanco sees Nacional branches integrated in Feb. \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Aug 13 (Reuter) - Brazilian private bank Unibanco expects to complete the process of fully integrating the 568 branch outlets belonging to failed Banco Nacional to its own network by February 1997, a top bank executive said. \par \par \uc2  "We have already fully integrated 60 branches and we plan to integrate 88 more in August, some 80 in September and finalize the process early February next year," Adalberto de Moraes Schettert, Unibanco's vice-president, told reporters on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In November 1995, Unibanco took over selected assets and liabilities of Banco Nacional, which was among \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top 10 banks, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the bank. \par \par \uc2  Schettert said so far Unibanco has unified the automatic teller machines system, bank cards, Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He also said Unibanco had set aside some 160-165 million reais, of which 40 percent has already been spent, to cover expenses with the acquisition of the healthy portion of Nacional. \par \par \uc2  He expects the remaining 60 percent will be enough to complete the process of uniting the two banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Unibanco, Brazil's third-largest private bank, announced late Monday a 126.9 million real net profit for the first six months of the year, an increase of 83.3 percent when compared with the same period of 1995. \par \par \uc2  The bank showed a 12.77 percent return on assets in the first half, with a net worth of 2.048 billion reais and total assets of 23.4 billion reais, Unibanco said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Unibanco said the bank's dividends totalled 42.2 million reais, which is equivalent to 35 percent of its net profit. \par \par \uc2  -- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55d-11-2324411 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds8d048nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
