\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil's real tumbles 0.48 pct on Argentine rumor. \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, July 31 (Reuter) - Brazil's real tumbled 0.48 percent, closing at 1.0150 per dollar in the commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, in nervous trade following a rumor that Argentina would end its peso/dollar parity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Traders here speculated the rumor was fueled by players hoping to profit by a market stir ahead of today's expiry of interest rate and dollar future contracts. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market remained jittery even though newly named Argentine Economy Minister Roque Fernandez denied he was considering altering the parity. \par \par \uc2  "A denial like this is worth nothing," a dealer said, noting that former Economy Minister Domingo Cavallo was sacked last Friday just a few hours after Argentine officials had denied his resignation. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to calm the market by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  five times in the floating \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The real closed up 0.19 percent at 1.0120 to the dollar in the floating market. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders expect nervousness to continue at Thursday's open. \par \par \uc2  "To calm down the (\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the commercial market," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The rumor led Brazil's futures \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to trade 696,640 contracts, an increase of 76 percent over Tuesday's volume. \par \par \uc2  September dollar contracts closed at 1,025 points, up 0.67 percent, while October contracts rose 0.8 percent, ending at 1,0335 points. \par \par \uc2  In the illegal parallel market, the real closed steady at 1.034 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds7v04uoz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
