\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Dollar Flat At 97.2 Centavos On Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 1995\par 21:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (AP-DJ)--The U.S. dollar was flat Thursday at 97.2 centavos on \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with one \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At closing, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were quoting the dollar at a buy rate of 97.21 centavos and a sell rate of 97.20 centavos at the commercial rate, virtually the same as on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on the floating exchange to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down on that market. The floating rate is used for personal remittances, while the commercial rate is for foreign trade and investment. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to force down the floating rate whenever it surpasses the commercial rate. \par \par \uc2  On June 22, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a new exchange rate band for the dollar of 91-99 centavos, from a previous range of 88-93 centavos. The move is seen as allowing the real to continue its gradual devaluation against the dollar. At the end of 1994, the dollar was trading at around 85 centavos on Brazil's commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Since then, several mini-devaluations of the real have nudged the dollar upward in small increments. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-12-95 \par \par \uc2  2034GMT \